1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:05,200
Import your collection. A CSV or Excel file with a header row. One item per row. About 3 minutes.

2
00:00:06,100 --> 00:00:15,600
Open Import. In your Vault, open Tools and choose Import.

3
00:00:16,600 --> 00:00:26,100
Choose your spreadsheet. Choose Upload Spreadsheet and pick your CSV or Excel file.

4
00:00:27,100 --> 00:00:36,600
Check the summary. See items ready, total cost, total value and anything that needs a look.

5
00:00:37,600 --> 00:00:47,100
Review duplicates and warnings. Exact duplicates are listed. Nothing unclear is guessed.

6
00:00:48,100 --> 00:00:57,600
Check the column mapping. Confirm each column is mapped to the right field.

7
00:00:58,600 --> 00:01:08,100
Choose how to handle duplicates. For example, skip exact duplicate titles within this batch.

8
00:01:09,100 --> 00:01:18,600
Confirm. Choose Review and Confirm Import, then confirm. You will see what was imported and skipped.

9
00:01:19,600 --> 00:01:29,100
See your items. Your imported items are now in your Vault.

10
00:01:30,100 --> 00:01:36,000
Your spreadsheet items are in your Vault. Next: add photos to your imported items.
